APAC IBM STORAGE PROTECT 8.1.25 – RHEL TO AIX MIGRATION Change Main
Points + Technical Execution Notes
================================================

PURPOSE Migrate APAC IBM Storage Protect 8.1.25 from legacy RHEL host
ODLPGRA1 to AIX host p3lah002 (instance splpgra1). Existing APAC archive
data remains in the current HCP namespace. The SP database/configuration
is migrated using EXTRACTDB / LOADFORMAT / INSERTDB. The RHEL source
remains stopped and unchanged during target validation and is restarted
only if backout is required.

================================================ 1. MAIN POINTS FOR THE
CHANGE RECORD ================================================

1.  Pre-change readiness

-   Verify splpgra1, AIX filesystems and capacity.
-   Prepare dsmserv.opt, dsm.opt and dsm.sys.
-   Securely prepare/copy dsmkeydb.kdb and dsmkeydb.sth.
-   Prepare HCP certificate (hcp.arm / applicable certificate).
-   Verify DNS and TLS/network connectivity from AIX to APAC HCP.

2.  Source preparation

-   Verify source DB/log/server health.
-   Remove obsolete metadata for retired SnapLock storage.
-   Remove obsolete storage pool after dependencies are cleared.
-   Set ARCHIVERETENTIONPROTECTION ON and verify.

3.  Recovery protection

-   Perform a new FULL SP database backup.
-   Save DEVCONFIG and VOLHISTORY.
-   Confirm successful completion before continuing.

4.  Freeze and PRE evidence

-   DISABLE SESSIONS ALL and drain relevant sessions/processes.
-   Generate complete, deterministically sorted ARCHIVES metadata
    manifest.
-   Generate SHA-256 fingerprint.
-   Capture nodes, filespaces, occupancy, archive count and
    damaged-object status.

5.  Source stop and database extract

-   Perform final source health check.
-   HALT source server and record freeze timestamp.
-   Run validated EXTRACTDB.
-   Verify extract/manifest and generate transfer checksums.

6.  Transfer to AIX

-   SCP extract, manifest and checksum files to p3lah002.
-   Verify file integrity before continuing.

7.  Target database build

-   Recheck target config, certificate and dsmkeydb files.
-   Run DSMSERV LOADFORMAT.
-   Run DSMSERV INSERTDB.
-   Start splpgra1 without enabling production traffic.

8.  Target validation

-   Verify server/DB/log health and ACTLOG.
-   Run VALIDATE CLOUD against existing APAC HCP.
-   HCP validation failure = NO-GO.

9.  Metadata reconciliation

-   Generate POST ARCHIVES manifest using exactly the same SELECT/ORDER
    BY as PRE.
-   Compare PRE/POST counts, complete files and SHA-256 values.
-   Compare nodes/filespaces/occupancy.
-   Confirm no new damaged objects and retention protection remains ON.
-   Any unexplained metadata difference = NO-GO.

10. Application cutover [L3]

-   Point APAC CMOD to new AIX SP endpoint.
-   Enable required sessions.
-   Test representative historical retrievals: CMOD -> AIX SP ->
    existing HCP.
-   Review sessions, ACTLOG and final server health.

11. Completion [L3]

-   Accept only after technical validation, 100% metadata reconciliation
    and CMOD tests.
-   Keep ODLPGRA1 stopped and unchanged.
-   Decommissioning is outside this change.

================================================ 2. DETAILED TECHNICAL
EXECUTION ================================================

PHASE A – TARGET READINESS [L3/L2]

A1. Target environment [L3/L2]: su - splpgra1 id db2level

A2. Capacity [L3/L2]: df -g

Verify DB, active log, archive log, instance and staging capacity.

A3. Configuration [L3/L2]: ls -la

Verify: dsmserv.opt dsm.opt dsm.sys

A4. Master encryption key files [L3]: dsmkeydb.kdb dsmkeydb.sth

Verify: ls -la /dsmkeydb.*

Handle as sensitive key material and preserve required
ownership/permissions.

A5. HCP certificate [L3/L2]: ls -la

A6. DNS [L3/L2]: nslookup

A7. Network/TLS [L3/L2]: curl -v https:///

This is only connectivity validation. Storage Protect access is
validated later with VALIDATE CLOUD.

PHASE B – SOURCE CLEANUP AND HEALTH [L3; health/evidence queries may be
L3/L2]

B1. Capture [L3/L2]: q status q db f=d q log f=d q stgpool f=d q damaged

B2. Identify obsolete SnapLock definitions [L3] using relevant APAC
storage/container queries.

B3. Remove obsolete metadata [L3]:

B4. Remove obsolete pool [L3]:

B5. Enable retention protection [L3]: set archiveretentionprotection on
q status

Expected: Archive Retention Protection = ON.

PHASE C – RECOVERY PROTECTION [L3/L2]

C1. Full DB backup [L3/L2]: backup db type=full devclass=

C2. Verify [L3/L2]: q process q volhistory type=dbbackup

Successful current full backup is a GO/NO-GO prerequisite.

C3. DEVCONFIG [L3/L2]: backup devconfig
filenames=/devconfig_APAC_pre_migration

C4. VOLHISTORY [L3/L2]: backup volhistory
filenames=/volhist_APAC_pre_migration

PHASE D – FREEZE AND FINAL PRE EVIDENCE [L3/L2; L3 coordinates freeze]

D1. Freeze new sessions [L3/L2; L3 coordinates]: disable sessions all

D2. Drain/check [L3/L2]: q session q process

D3. Total archive count [L3/L2]: select count(*) as TOTAL_ARCHIVES from
archives

D4. Determine final ARCHIVES manifest columns [L3 defines; L2 may
execute]: select colname from syscat.columns where tabname=‘ARCHIVES’
order by colno

Create a complete PRE manifest using an approved SELECT with enough
metadata to identify every archive object and a deterministic ORDER BY.

Output: APAC_ARCHIVES_PRE.txt

D5. Fingerprint [L3/L2]: sha256sum APAC_ARCHIVES_PRE.txt >
APAC_ARCHIVES_PRE.sha256 wc -l APAC_ARCHIVES_PRE.txt

D6. Nodes [L3/L2]: select node_name,domain_name from nodes order by
node_name

D7. Filespaces [L3/L2]: select node_name,filespace_name,filespace_id
from filespaces order by node_name,filespace_name,filespace_id

D8. Additional evidence [L3/L2]: q occupancy q damaged

D9. Final source check [L3/L2]: q session q process q db f=d q log f=d

PHASE E – SOURCE STOP AND EXTRACT [L3]

E1. Stop [L3]: halt

Record exact SOURCE FREEZE TIMESTAMP.

IMPORTANT: ODLPGRA1 must not be restarted after this point unless
Backout is invoked.

E2. Extract [L3]:

Expected: - successful EXTRACTDB - extract files and manifest produced -
no fatal/failed migration messages

E3. Verify [L3/L2]: ls -lh

E4. Checksums [L3/L2]: sha256sum > APAC_EXTRACT.sha256

PHASE F – TRANSFER TO AIX [L3/L2]

F1. Transfer [L3/L2]: scp splpgra1@p3lah002:/

F2. Transfer manifest/checksums [L3/L2]: scp APAC_EXTRACT.sha256
splpgra1@p3lah002:/

F3. Validate on AIX [L3/L2]: cd sha256sum -c APAC_EXTRACT.sha256

All files must validate. Failure = NO-GO.

PHASE G – TARGET DATABASE BUILD [L3]

G1. Recheck [L3/L2]: su - splpgra1 df -g ls -la ls -la /dsmkeydb.* ls
