================================================ 4. BACKOUT PLAN

Backout ownership: L3 coordinates and owns the rollback decision.
Individual verification and instance-owner tasks may be executed by L2
when explicitly directed by L3.

Invoke backout if mandatory technical validation, metadata
reconciliation or application validation fails before final acceptance.

1.  Block target: disable sessions all

2.  Stop target: halt or

3.  Restore CMOD endpoint:

4.  Start ODLPGRA1:

5.  Validate: q status q db f=d q log f=d q stgpool f=d

6.  Restore access: enable sessions all

7.  Test historical CMOD retrieval through original RHEL SP.

8.  Review: q actlog begindate=today

9.  Record rollback evidence.

Backout principle: The source remains stopped and unchanged throughout
target build/validation and is restarted only when backout is invoked.
This preserves the pre-migration source state.

